Imports:
  - Types:
      - Storage
      - MetricRow
      - OpenOptions
    From: lib/storage

Usages:
  thin_wrapper: |
    Of the three storage-facing app packages (vminsert does protocol parsing/relabeling/routing,
    vmselect does query planning/merging, vmstorage is this cell), vmstorage is the thinnest:
    nearly every meaningful exported operation (WriteRows, SearchMetricNames, DeleteSeries,
    LabelValues, TSDBStatus, snapshot management) is a near 1:1 pass-through to the
    corresponding lib/storage.Storage method, wrapped only by request-draining
    (WaitGroup Add/Done for graceful shutdown) and, for vmselect-facing calls, a tenant-ID
    validation/prefixing wrapper. In this pinned commit, app/vmstorage is a library (package
    vmstorage, not package main) consumed by the single-node app/victoria-metrics binary's
    main(), not an independently built entry point of its own — cluster deployments still
    package it as a separately named "vmstorage" artifact built from the same underlying source.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the direct network/admin-facing wrapper around one `Storage` instance: it opens
  the engine at startup, exposes package-level function variables (VMInsertAPI, VMSelectAPI,
  GetSearch/PutSearch) that other components call to reach the storage engine, and — only
  when a -vmselectAddr flag is configured — starts an RPC server so a networked vmselect process
  can reach this instance's data.

  Use `thin_wrapper` to understand how little independent logic lives in this cell versus how
  much is pure delegation to `Storage`.

  Use `MetricRow` and `OpenOptions` from Imports to see the two lib/storage types this cell's
  own contract is expressed in terms of.

---

"Init(vmselectMaxConcurrentRequests: int, vmselectMaxQueueDuration: time.Duration, resetCacheIfNeeded: CacheResetCallback)":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Configure and open the storage engine, then (only if a vmselect-facing network address is
    configured) start an RPC server for it.

    `resetCacheIfNeeded`: callback the caller (query layer) supplies to invalidate its own
    result caches when new data invalidates them

    Algorithm:
    1. Apply all storage.Set*/mergeset.Set* package-level tuning knobs from CLI flags
    2. Build an `OpenOptions` from CLI flags (retention, max daily/hourly series limits, etc.)
       and call the `Storage` factory to open the engine at the configured data path
    3. Wrap the opened `Storage` in this cell's own `VMStorage`, exposing it via the
       package-level VMInsertAPI/VMSelectAPI/GetSearch/PutSearch variables
    4. If -vmselectAddr is set, start a vmselect-facing RPC server backed by a tenant-scoped
       wrapper around the same `VMStorage`

"Stop()":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Stop any running vmselect RPC server, drain in-flight requests, close the underlying
    `Storage`, and stop background maintenance (e.g. the stale-snapshot remover).

"DataPath() -> path:string":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Return the configured on-disk data directory for this storage instance.

"VMStorage(s: Storage)":
  location: vmstorage.go
  annotations: |
    Wraps one `Storage` instance and implements the API surface consumed by both the insert side
    and the select side of the system (see `thin_wrapper`). Constructed once at `Init` time and
    referenced only through the package-level VMInsertAPI/VMSelectAPI variables afterward.

    Snapshot administration (create/list/delete) is handled directly in this cell's own admin
    HTTP endpoints (main.go) by calling the wrapped `Storage`'s snapshot methods inline — it is
    not exposed as a method of this type.
  methods:
    "WriteRows(rows: []MetricRow) -> err:error": |
      Forward `rows` to the underlying `Storage`'s AddRows method.
    "IsReadOnly() -> readOnly:bool": |
      Forward to `Storage`'s IsReadOnly method.
    "SearchMetricNames(qt: QueryTracer, sq: SearchQuery, deadline: uint64) -> names:[]string, err:error": |
      Resolve `sq`'s tag filters and forward to `Storage`'s SearchMetricNames method.
    "DeleteSeries(qt: QueryTracer, sq: SearchQuery, deadline: uint64) -> deleted:int, err:error": |
      Resolve `sq`'s tag filters and forward to `Storage`'s DeleteSeries method.
    "TSDBStatus(qt: QueryTracer, sq: SearchQuery, focusLabel: string, topN: int, deadline: uint64) -> status:TSDBStatus, err:error": |
      Resolve `sq`'s tag filters and forward to `Storage`'s GetTSDBStatus method.
    "Stop()": |
      Drain in-flight requests, stop this wrapper's own background goroutine (stale-snapshot
      removal), then close the underlying `Storage`.

"VMStorage::VMStorageWithTenantID(accountID: uint32, projectID: uint32)":
  location: vmstorage_with_tenant_id.go
  annotations: |
    Tenant-scoping specialization of `VMStorage`, installed as the API implementation handed to
    the vmselect-facing RPC server. Every method validates the caller's tenant token (against
    the configured `accountID`/`projectID` or a request-supplied multi-tenant token) before
    delegating to the wrapped `VMStorage`, and re-marshals results with tenant-ID-prefixed
    metric names/blocks.

